  "question": "What owns table topology, cell coordinates, selection, clipboard and layout?",
  "model": "GPT-6 / Codex",
  "method": "Best API Review; Redesign from First Principles; Benchmark three-lane owner comparison; production adoption and native closure",
  "trigger": "Execute the revalidated table host-delivery benchmark, select the least-general passing owner, adopt it completely, and perform a harsh final omission audit.",
  "requirements": [
    "Keep table geometry, span closure, exact sparse cells, row/table projection and held native ranges in Plate while using the mounted view host lifetime.",
    "Preserve complete render.useViewElementAttributes delivery through React props and avoid a generic public host channel unless it proves an independent job.",
    "Replace the public painter only after long-lived no-GC owner, production mount/paint and native correctness evidence pass frozen budgets.",
    "Use one visible cell selection layer, support same-key host replacement and cleanup, and require custom cells to forward the canonical attributes/ref exactly once."
  ],
  "evidenceReuse": "Reused prior canonical-selection, authored-root and semantic projection adoption because their current owners and requirements remain unchanged. Repaired and retained the current painter as the production baseline. Rebuilt and reran every candidate browser packet after the final omission audit deleted the surviving copied row/table overlay owner; no stale candidate result is promoted.",
  "summary": "Stop further host-delivery redesign and retain the adopted private TablePlugin binder. One per-view projection writes only affected canonical cell hosts, the public useTableSelectionDOM hook and copied row/table overlay owner are deleted, and render.useViewElementAttributes remains unchanged. The binder passes all four 30-packet no-GC owner cohorts, every production Chromium paint/mount budget, and 14/14 native table cases. The explicit scalar channel and Plite markers add public machinery without an independent job.",
  "verdict": "stop",
  "previous": "2026-09-17-table-host-delivery-model-revalidation",
  "relation": "reverses",
  "alternatives": [
    "Keep the repaired painter: rejected after the private binder preserved behavior, fixed same-key replacement and removed per-table projection/query fanout.",
    "Publish an explicit scalar-only host channel: rejected because the private owner passes every budget and wins fanout without changing public React prop semantics.",
    "Redefine render.useViewElementAttributes as host-only or split it by attribute spelling: rejected because custom component props are a real existing job and no migration benefit is earned.",
    "Promote selected-cell markers or table selection verbs into Plite: rejected because span closure, row/table expansion and held-range projection are Plate table semantics.",
    "Keep copied row/table overlay context beside the binder: rejected in the final omission audit because it creates a second visible selection owner.",
    "Adopt one private TablePlugin projection and canonical cell-host binder, delete duplicate owners, and preserve the public callback: adopted."
  ],
  "proofLimits": "The owner probe uses Happy DOM with real source and 360 actions per lane/cohort; native claims come from production Chromium. Selection uses 110 raw paint samples per browser cohort. Mount uses distributions of per-process packet p95 values because raw remount samples were not serialized. One mounted view supports one canonical host per node key; custom cells must forward the supplied ref exactly once. Broad table partition typecheck remains blocked by unrelated authored TS6307 project-file-list errors, with no changed-file diagnostic. No physical-device, publication or release claim is made.",
